---
description: Never print or commit secrets. mcp.json and .env files stay out of git.
globs: "**/*"
alwaysApply: true
---

# Secrets

- Never print secret values (tokens, passwords, API keys, publishable keys when paired with private context) in chat, commits, logs, or docs.
- Never commit `.env`, `.env.local`, or any real credential file.
- `.cursor/mcp.json` is gitignored — it may hold local MCP tokens; do not force-add it.
- Commit only `.env.example` with placeholder names, never real values.
- CI secrets live in GitHub Environments (`staging` / `production`). Local `.env.local` is staging-only.
- Prefer referring to secrets by **name** (e.g. `SUPABASE_ACCESS_TOKEN`) when debugging.
